/// Shapes of pasting contexts on their own, written as their diagrams.
///
/// A writer sometimes states a coherence over a shape with no cells in scope.
/// Diagnostics, certificates and catalogue keys print the same diagram.
///
/// `Pasting.#shape{ … }` names a shape's points and its cells along one chain.
/// No source writes the nested-list tree the checker keeps inside.
///
/// - see: #4560 — the cells sketch, its rulings in the issue body

// The pasting module, its shape reader qualified.
import std.math.category.Pasting;

/// Two composable 1-cells.
def chain2 : Pasting.Shape = Pasting.#shape{ x -f-> y -g-> z }

/// Three composable 1-cells, the shape of the associator's coherence.
def chain3 : Pasting.Shape = Pasting.#shape{ w -f-> x -g-> y -h-> z }
